      "content": "That feeling of being a walking corpse is a profound and utterly exhausting experience, and it speaks to the deep wound you are carrying. When the foundation feels gone, sometimes the first step isn't rebuilding, but finding a small, quiet space *outside* of the wreckage for yourself. Therapists can help you find moments of internal quiet, even amidst the external noise, to start acknowledging small pieces of yourself that remain. Please consider reaching out to someone who can help you hold the weight of all this right now.",
